@startuml Linkwise_Chat_IBD
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "Latin Modern Roman"
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam ArrowColor #2A9D8F
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam nodesep 22
skinparam ranksep 28
title SysML-style ibd: station interfaces and data flow (proposed)
top to bottom direction
rectangle "agent : AgentHost" as Agent <<part>>
rectangle "localStation : LinkwiseStation" {
 rectangle "mcp : MessagingAdapter\nprovided: ChatService" as MCP <<part>>
 rectangle "messages : MessagingService" as Msg <<part>>
 database "spool : DurableStore" as Store
 rectangle "execution : StationExecution\nrequired: ModemSessionPort" as Exec <<part>>
 rectangle "modem : ModemBackend" as Modem <<part>>
 rectangle "audio : AudioAdapter" as Audio <<part>>
 rectangle "ptt : ArbiterAndWatchdog" as PTT <<part>>
}
rectangle "radio : Transceiver" as Radio <<part>>
rectangle "peer : RemoteStation" as Peer <<part>>
Agent --> MCP : typed requests / cursor\nevents
MCP --> Msg : validated application\ncommands
Msg <--> Store : bounded bodies / durable\ntransactions
Msg --> Exec : route intent + message\nreferences
Exec --> Modem : lifecycle / bounded byte\nstream
Exec --> PTT : locally authorized keying
Modem <--> Audio : continuous PCM + completion\nevidence
Audio <--> Radio : receive / transmit audio
PTT --> Radio : exclusive PTT / release
Radio <--> Peer : HF channel
note bottom of Msg
Envelope bytes use bounded streams/spools below MCP.
Station preparation, lease and grant checks remain
authoritative.
Interfaces shown are contracts, not formal SysML
port declarations.
end note
@enduml
